 * and confidence maturity.
 *
 * Amendment 1 rule: superseded records are DOWN-WEIGHTED, not hard-filtered —
 * a superseded record stays reachable so recall can still surface "there is a
 * newer correction here" instead of going silent, and so the index knows the
 * record exists. ACL (visibility/sensitivity) is the *only* hard gate and runs
 * before scoring (a later slice). Neither status nor confidence ever zeroes a
 * candidate out; the smallest multiplier this module produces is still > 0.
